<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Salazar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1508–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Juan de Salazar de Espinosa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de Salazar de Espinosa was a Spanish conquistador who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>, on 15 August 1537 as a fort on the Paraguay river, during the search for the missing explorer Juan de Ayolas. The fort became the centre of Spanish settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> region after the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> was abandoned in 1541.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-de-salazar.jpg" alt="Juan de Salazar" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iwan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JuanDeSalazar.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
